From 253d3fae31b199741ad4aec149e2e8e48fa825f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Huang <shuang@myai001.mylab.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:04:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] chore(dsv4): kill switch and one-shot trace for the
 parallel top-K

The parallel top-K was measured end to end by restarting the server with one
environment variable flipped, which is a fine way to attribute a regression --
or to exonerate a change, which is what it was needed for here. Baking the
switch into the launcher instead of into the code means going back and forth
does not require an edit.

SGLANG_OPT_SM75_PARALLEL_TOPK=0 restores the single-program kernel.
SGLANG_OPT_SM75_TOPK_DIAG=1 logs, once per shape, the width and row count the
dispatch actually sees and which path it chose. That log is the only trustworthy
record of what a worker did: the schedulers rename themselves with
setproctitle, so /proc/<pid>/environ reports the environment they were forked
with, not the one they are running under. Reading that as evidence produced a
confident and wrong conclusion once already.
